          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong comonad
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %em cotriple
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoid"} comonoid
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            of endofunctors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoid"} comonoid
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(X,X)
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\in K
          %p
            Just as a monad may be defined for any 2-category,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+2-functor"} lax 2-functor
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1}
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+2-functor"} oplax 2-functor
            from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{1} \to E
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            for more.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#coalgebras Coalgebras
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebra+over+a+comonad"} coalgebra over a comonad
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong comodule
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            with a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\to C a
            satisfying dual axioms to those for an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebra over a monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+category"} Eilenberg-Moore category
            and satisfies a universal property dual to that of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Moore+object"} Eilenberg-Moore object
            for a monad; it can thereby be internalized to any
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from the category of coalgebras to the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is called a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonadic+functor"} comonadic functor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Kleisli+category"} co-Kleisli category
          %h3#comonadic_homology_and_descent Comonadic homology and descent
          %p
            Any comonad on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            induces an augmented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            consisting of its iterates. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            and the comonad is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+monad"} additive
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                comonadic homology
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/comonadic+homology"} ?
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+for+a+monad"} Comodules
            (= coalgebras) over the comonad with underlying endofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi R
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi R
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_R\mapsto M_R\otimes_R S
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
            for the extension of rings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\hookrightarrow S
            correspond to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            data for that extension.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/zoranskoda/show/gluing+categories+from+localizations"} Gluing of categories from localizations
            may also be formalized via comonads.
          %h3#mixed_distributive_laws Mixed distributive laws
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} Distributive laws
            between a monad and a comonad are so-called
            %em mixed
            distributive laws; a special case has been rediscovered in physics under the name
            %em entwining structures
            (Brzeziński, Majid 1997). Their theory is often studied in the connection with the theory of comonads in the bicategory of rings, modules and morphisms of modules, that is
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coring"} coring
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "http://front.math.ucdavis.edu/0805.4611"} Škoda 2008
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} comp
            (R. Street,
            = succeed "," do
              %em Formal theory of monads
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/necessity"} necessity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/writer+comonad"} writer comonad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/store+comonad"} store comonad
            %li
              %p
